  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDF Regulatory framework institutional capacity building for Cooperative sector in Morocco</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improve the legal environment for small producers to engage and benefit from market economy.  IDF Grant amount proposed will be below $500,000. 7/9/09.  Approved 3/11/09; Effective 5/13/09; IDF TF094209 Closing date: 5/13/2012. 5/6/10.  Task Team Leader changed from Pierre Rondot (UPI#113372) to Mohamed Medouar (UPI#265489) effective May 10, 2010. The main development objective of the grant is to help foster economic growth in Morocco by reinforcing the capacity and effectiveness of the cooperative sector through support in improving its regulatory framework, and by modernization of the institutions and services in charge, such as: the Ministry of Economic and General Affairs (MAEG), Office for the development of cooperation (ODCO), the technical departments of the line Ministries including Agriculture, Habitat, Handicraft, Fishery, Trade, Transport, National Forestry Commission etc , other semi-public organizations such as the Social Development Agency (ADS), national Mutual aid, Development agencies, and the National Federation of Cooperatives.</narrative>
  </description>
